Where it came from
------------------

This project began as a webcomic-downloading script written by AChillVamp:
https://archive.org/details/@achillvamp

The core of it is theirs. Their script worked out the loop that everything here still turns on: open
a comic's page in a browser, find the image by trying a list of likely element paths until one
matches, save it, press "next", and repeat. mirror_base.py is still built around that loop.

Everything else, including the library updater, the web page, chapters, .cbz packing and adopting
existing folders, was written later by ZornTaov, much of it with Anthropic's Claude. The element paths
and help text that shipped with the original have since been replaced.

If you are AChillVamp, or know how to reach them, please get in touch. We'll gladly change how they
are credited here if they would like it different.
